{"id": "DfR0f5exPc9", "title": "Video by therishikatha", "description": "Why did Parshurama go to war 21 times… and then give the WHOLE EARTH away? 🪓🌍 Part 5 of the Parshurama series.\n\nAfter Part 4, the sons of the thousand-armed king wanted revenge. While Rama was out fetching firewood, they came to the ashram. His father, Sage Jamadagni, was deep in tapas and would not fight. He called out \"Rama! Rama!\", and they killed him. Rama came back too late.\n\nHe lit his father's pyre and made a vow. Twenty-one times he fought the arrogant kings of the earth, until at Samantapanchaka his ancestors, led by Rishi Richika, appeared and said: \"We are pleased. Now be at peace.\" Those five lakes became holy, and the place is Kurukshetra, where the Mahabharata war was later fought.\n\nThen, at a great yagna, Parshurama gave the whole earth to Sage Kashyapa, who told him to leave his land, so he went south to the sea. And Kashyapa crowned the princes who had grown up hidden, among bears, cows and calves.\n\n📖 Source: Mahabharata, Vana Parva 116–117, Adi Parva 2 and Shanti Parva 49.\n\n📚 Stories of Shakti for little ones: the Navadurga Set from Rishi Katha is out now. Check the link in bio (rishikatha.com).\n\n💬 Why EXACTLY 21 times? Comment if you know (answer pinned 👇)\n🔁 Save it for Part 6 and share it with someone who loves Parshurama.\n\n#parshuram #parshurama #parashurama #jamadagni #kurukshetra #mahabharata #hindumythology #sanatandharma #vishnuavatar #dashavatar #indianmythology #puranas #mythologystories #rishikatha #hinduism", "channel": "therishikatha", "uploader_id": "22569163881", "uploader": "Rishi Katha", "timestamp": 1793706922, "like_count": 1967, "comment_count": 39, "http_headers": {"Referer": "https://www.instagram.com/"}, "formats": [{"format_id": "dash-1081773981351957a", "ext": "m4a", "tbr": 52.461, "asr": 48000, "format_note": "DASH audio", "container": "m4a_dash", "vcodec": "none", "acodec": "mp4a.40.5", "url": "https://instagram.fblr2-3.fna.fbcdn.ne